    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The third angle is also \\(60^\\circ,\\) so the triangle is equilateral with side \\(4.\\) Its area is \\[ \\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}(4)^2=4\\sqrt3. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Determine the third angle of the triangle",
        "Use the area formula for an equilateral triangle of side \\(4\\)"
